          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Differentiate the following functions by first principles.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=3x^2$\n\nExpand $(x+h)^3$ in the first-principles quotient.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(x+h)^3-x^3}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{3x^2h+3xh^2+h^3}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}(3x^2+3xh+h^2)\\\\f'(x)&=3x^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$, $x\\ne0$.\n\nCombine the fractions before taking the limit.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{x+h}-\\frac{1}{x}}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{x-(x+h)}{hx(x+h)}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-1}{x(x+h)}\\\\f'(x)&=-\\frac{1}{x^2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\dfrac{2}{x^3}$, $x\\ne0$.\n\nCombine the fractions and factor out $h$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{(x+h)^2}-\\frac{1}{x^2}}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{x^2-(x+h)^2}{hx^2(x+h)^2}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-2x-h}{x^2(x+h)^2}\\\\f'(x)&=-\\frac{2}{x^3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}$, $x>0$.\n\nRationalise the numerator of the difference quotient.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+h}-\\sqrt{x}}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(x+h)-x}{h(\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x})}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x}}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\dfrac{1}{2x^{3/2}}$, $x>0$.\n\nCombine the fractions, then rationalise the radical difference.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x+h}}{h\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x+h}}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x+h}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x+h})}\\\\f'(x)&=-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x}}=-\\frac{1}{2x^{3/2}}\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
